<title>CANADA: Two killed in Canadian motel explosion.</title>
<headline>Two killed in Canadian motel explosion.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER, British Columbia 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two men were killed and an eight-year-old boy was critically injured when an explosion ripped through a motel in British Columbia on Tuesday, officials said.</p>
<p>A fire department spokesman said investigators believed a propane leak caused the blast in the town of Kamloops, 220 miles (350 km) northeast of Vancouver.</p>
